.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY2_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json:584:      "raw_output": "src/pipd_ls_sp/validate.py:24:#   cannot sit inside the hash it references) and the `_profile_meta` sidecar. This is the\nsrc/pipd_ls_sp/validate.py:51:    Schema validation runs on a COPY of the record with the genuine non-record sidecars\nsrc/pipd_ls_sp/validate.py:60:    sidecar ``_profile_meta`` is stripped; the defensive \"unless the schema declares it\" guard\nsrc/pipd_ls_sp/validate.py:61:    keeps that safe even if a future schema chooses to declare a sidecar. This closes CE-2 without\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:28:   \"id\": \"TT-S4POST-F04-CROSS-RECORD-PERMISSION\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:32:   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"validate_bundle accepts a self-consistent but rehashed permission expansion\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:35:   \"evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F04\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:41:   \"raw_evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F04\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:46:   \"id\": \"TT-S4POST-F05-SIDECAR-UNVALIDATED\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:48:   \"owner\": \"PKG-01 schemas (profile sidecar contract)\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:49:   \"affected_edges\": \"_profile_meta sidecar -> consumer claim interpretation\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:50:   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"non-record sidecar values are not validated\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:51:   \"detail\": \"Injecting LOW_RISK_VERIFIED, independent_acceptance=PASS and allowed_claims=[PRODUCTION_VERIFIED] into PI-PKG._profile_meta validates with 0 findings, because the sidecar is stripped before schema validation by design. The compiled bundle emits NOT_ASSESSED and no LOW_RISK_VERIFIED, so the shipped artefact is correct; the risk is a consumer reading validation PASS as authority for sidecar values.\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:52:   \"close_condition\": \"either declare a minimal schema for the sidecar or state in the consumer documentation that PASS never authorises sidecar values\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:53:   \"evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F05\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:59:   \"raw_evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F05\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:60:   \"close_criterion\": \"either declare a minimal schema for the sidecar or state in the consumer documentation that PASS never authorises sidecar values\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:64:   \"id\": \"TT-S4POST-F06-EMPTY-TRACE\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:68:   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"an empty trace array is accepted\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:69:   \"detail\": \"Setting a compiled PI trace to [] yields bundle PASS without a rehash. The schema now enforces array typing and the item required-keys, which is exactly what POST-F03 asked for; it does not require non-empty trace or cross-record closu