.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY2_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json:598:      "raw_output": "{\r\n \"schema\": \"PIPD-TT-REGISTER/1\",\r\n \"scope\": \"round-scoped delta register — NOT merged into .hgk/artifacts/TT_REGISTER.json by this round\",\r\n \"round\": \"POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair\",\r\n \"as_of_candidate\": \"dbe387195d25aca32829f84c051b7bf52b5931eb\",\r\n \"merge_handoff\": \"the operator must fold these rows into .hgk/artifacts/TT_REGISTER.json and regenerate its status_summary via tools/tt_summary_check.py --write; merging was deliberately not done here because that register's projection is asserted by tests/test_tt_summary.py and is outside this round's write scope\",\r\n \"count\": 8,\r\n \"tts\": [\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"TT-S4POST-F02-HARNESS-ENV-DEPENDENCE\",\r\n   \"class\": \"TOOLING\",\r\n   \"owner\": \"PKG-08 packaging / DOC-07 verification\",\r\n   \"affected_edges\": \"post-release verification harness -> unittest discovery\",\r\n   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"full-suite pass is environment-dependent\",\r\n   \"detail\": \"10 test modules require git history or built artefacts (test_publication_projection needs a local frozen ref; test_wheel_distribution needs dist/; test_evidence_manifest, test_tooling_executes and test_atomic_requirements need a real checkout). Exported as a git archive with no .git, the PRE-REPAIR base commit 4445db5a already fails with the same 8 failures + 2 errors, so the profile predates this round and is not a regression. The independent checker could only observe the archive/clone environment because its own read-only rule forbade running in the candidate cwd, so it reported FAIL while the operator's checkout run reported 325 OK at base and 383 OK at the candidate.\",\r\n   \"close_condition\": \"the suite either becomes archive-safe (skip-module guards on the environment-dependent cases with a printed reason) or documents the required environment at the top of tests/; then an archive run and a checkout run agree\",\r\n   \"evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_F02_RESOLUTION.json\",\r\n   \"status\": \"OPEN\",\r\n   \"severity\": \"NON_BLOCKING\",\r\n   \"origin\": \"INDEPENDENT_VERIFY\",\r\n   \"state_round\": \"POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair\",\r\n   \"status_round\": \"dbe387195d25aca32829f84c051b7bf52b5931eb\",\r\n   \"raw_evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_F02_RESOLUTION.json\",\r\n   \"close_criterion\": \"the suite either becomes archive-safe (skip-module guards on the environment-dependent cases with a printed reason) or documents the required environment at the top of tests/; then an archive run and a checkout run agree\",\r\n   \"closed_requires_fresh_verification\": true\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"TT-S4POST-F04-CROSS-RECORD-PERMISSION\",\r\n   \"class\": \"CONTRACT_GAP\",\r\n   \"owner\": \"PKG-01 schemas + PKG-05 ECP/receiver handoff\",\r\n   \"affected_edges\": \"ECP.permission.scope -> PD writable scope -> receiver handoff\",\r\n   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"validate_bundle accepts a self-consistent but rehashed permission expansion\",\r\n   \"detail\": \"An independently re-hashed record whose ECP.permission.scope was widened from src/** to ** still validates PASS with 0 findings, because content_hash proves the record is internally consistent and not that it agrees with the bound PD scope. No executor was invoked and no permission was actually granted; this is a contract-closure gap rather than an exercised escalation.\",\r\n   \"close_condition\": \"validate_bundle emits a SEMANTIC finding when an ECP permission scope is broader than the PD scope it is bound to, with POS/NEG fixtures\",\r\n   \"evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F04\",\r\n   \"status\": \"OPEN\",\r\n   \"severity\": \"BLOCKER\",\r\n   \"origin\": \"INDEPENDENT_VERIFY\",\r\n   \"state_round\": \"POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair\",\r\n   \"status_round\": \"dbe387195d25aca32829f84c051b7bf52b5931eb\",\r\n   \"raw_evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F04\",\r\n   \"close_criterion\": \"validate_bundle emits a SEMANTIC finding when an ECP permission scope is broader than the PD scope it is bound to, with POS/NEG fixtures\",\r\n   \"closed_requires_fresh_verification\": true\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"TT-S4POST-F05-SIDECAR-UNVALIDATED\",\r\n   \"class\": \"CONTRACT_GAP\",\r\n   \"owner\": \"PKG-01 schemas (profile sidecar contract)\",\r\n   \"affected_edges\": \"_profile_meta sidecar -> consumer claim interpretation\",\r\n   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"non-record sidecar values are not validated\",\r\n   \"detail\": \"Injecting LOW_RISK_VERIFIED, independent_acceptance=PASS and allowed_claims=[PRODUCTION_VERIFIED] into PI-PKG._profile_meta validates with 0 findings, because the sidecar is stripped before schema validation by design. The compiled bundle emits NOT_ASSESSED and no LOW_RISK_VERIFIED, so the shipped artefact is correct; the risk is a consumer reading validation PASS as authority for sidecar values.\",\r\n   \"close_condition\": \"either declare a minimal schema for the sidecar or state in the consumer documentation that PASS never authorises sidecar values\",\r\n   \"evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F05\",\r\n   \"status\": \"OPEN\",\r\n   \"severity\": \"NON_BLOCKING\",\r\n   \"origin\": \"INDEPENDENT_VERIFY\",\r\n   \"state_round\": \"POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair\",\r\n   \"status_round\": \"dbe387195d25aca32829f84c051b7bf52b5931eb\",\r\n   \"raw_evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F05\",\r\n   \"close_criterion\": \"either declare a minimal schema for the sidecar or state in the consumer documentation that PASS never authorises sidecar values\",\r\n   \"closed_requires_fresh_verification\": true\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"TT-S4POST-F06-EMPTY-TRACE\",\r\n   \"class\": \"CONTRACT_GAP\",\r\n   \"owner\": \"PKG-01 schemas (PI trace shape)\",\r\n   \"affected_edges\": \"PI-PKG.trace -> traceability assurance\",\r\n   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"an empty trace array is accepted\",\r\n   \"detail\": \"Setting a compiled PI trace to [] yields bundle PASS without a rehash. The schema now enforces array typing and the item required-keys, which is exactly what POST-F03 asked for; it does not require non-empty trace or cross-record closure. Reported as the observed limit of validate_bundle, not as an executor bypass.\",\r\n   \"close_condition\": \"add a minItems/cross-record closure rule for trace only if the upstream contract requires it, with POS/NEG fixtures\",\r\n   \"evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F06\",\r\n   \"status\": \"OPEN\",\r\n   \"severity\": \"NON_BLOCKING\",\r\n   \"origin\": \"INDEPENDENT_VERIFY\",\r\n   \"state_round\": \"POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair\",\r\n   \"status_round\": \"dbe387195d25aca32829f84c051b7bf52b5931eb\",\r\n   \"raw_evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F06\",\r\n   \"close_criterion\": \"add a minItems/cross-record closure rule for trace only if the upstream contract requires it, with POS/NEG fixtures\",\r\n   \"closed_requires_fresh_verification\": true\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"TT-S4POST-F07-VERSION-IDENTITY\",\r\n   \"class\": \"UX\",\r\n   \"owner\": \"PKG-08 packaging / Owner release decision\",\r\n   \"affected_edges\": \"wheel filename -> distribution METADATA -> tag -> README\",\r\n   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"preview.1 and preview.2 ship the same distribution version 0.1.0\",\r\n   \"detail\": \"Both prereleases are pipd_ls_sp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl with different hashes, so pip upgrade/cache resolution and user support threads cannot distinguish them by version. The released tag is immutable and was NOT rewritten. The next patch must carry a PEP 440-legal version higher than 0.1.0 (e.g. 0.1.1b1 with tag v0.1.1-preview.1) with wheel name, METADATA, entry point, tag and README made consistent.\",\r\n   \"close_condition\": \"an owner-authorised successor prerelease ships a distinct distribution version, verified by an isolated-venv old->new upgrade, uninstall and rollback\",\r\n   \"evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/POST_F_DISPOSITION.json#POST-F07\",\r\n   \"status\": \"OPEN_OWNER_GATE\",\r\n   \"severity\": \"NON_BLOCKING\",\r\n   \"origin\": \"INDEPENDENT_VERIFY\",\r\n   \"state_round\": \"POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair\",\r\n   \"status_round\": \"dbe387195d25aca32829f84c051b7bf52b5931eb\",\r\n   \"raw_evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/POST_F_DISPOSITION.json#POST-F07\",\r\n   \"close_criterion\": \"an owner-authorised successor prerelease ships a distinct distribution version, verified by an isolated-venv old->new upgrade, uninstall and rollback\",\r\n   \"closed_requires_fresh_verification\": true\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"TT-S4POST-F09-INDEPENDENT-BUNDLE\",\r\n   \"class\": \"EVIDENCE_GAP\",\r\n   \"owner\": \"challenge-review bundle owner\",\r\n   \"affected_edges\": \"external challenge -> skill-native acceptance bundle\",\r\n   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"no skill-native full-scope challenge bundle exists\",\r\n   \"detail\": \"The native challenge-review bundle (references/evidence-intake.md, gate-calibration.md, finding-contract.md, the report template and scripts/verify_review_bundle.py) was not available in either the reporter's or this round's environment, so no native EXTERNAL_CHALLENGE_REPORT.json was produced. This round's checker wrote a scoped receipt instead and explicitly refused to claim FULL_S0_S4_INDEPENDENT_PASS.\",\r\n   \"close_condition\": \"provide the challenge bundle, then produce and schema-validate the native report for a frozen subject\",\r\n   \"evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json\",\r\n   \"status\": \"OPEN\",\r\n   \"severity\": \"NON_BLOCKING\",\r\n   \"origin\": \"INDEPENDENT_VERIFY\",\r\n   \"state_round\": \"POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair\",\r\n   \"status_round\": \"dbe387195d25aca32829f84c051b7bf52b5931eb\",\r\n   \"raw_evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json\",\r\n   \"close_criterion\": \"provide the challenge bundle, then produce and schema-validate the native report for a frozen subject\",\r\n   \"closed_requires_fresh_verification\": true\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"TT-S4POST-F10-S5-DEFERRED\",\r\n   \"class\": \"SCOPE\",\r\n   \"owner\": \"S5-S8 owner\",\r\n   \"affected_edges\": \"S4 plugin -> HGK live receiver / GENIE / JIT / SWOF\",\r\n   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"S5+ live surfaces are absent\",\r\n   \"detail\": \"Deliberately out of scope: HGK live receiver, GENIE product compiler, JIT factory, the 22 unselected technology candidates and the commercial signing pipeline belong to S5-S8 and are not made a fake prerequisite of this S4 patch.\",\r\n   \"close_condition\": \"S5 admission freezes its own subject, authority and evidence\",\r\n   \"evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/POST_F_DISPOSITION.json#POST-F10\",\r\n   \"status\": \"OPEN_OWNER_GATE\",\r\n   \"severity\": \"NON_BLOCKING\",\r\n   \"origin\": \"ORDER_SCOPE\",\r\n   \"state_round\": \"POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair\",\r\n   \"status_round\": \"dbe387195d25aca32829f84c051b7bf52b5931eb\",\r\n   \"raw_evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/POST_F_DISPOSITION.json#POST-F10\",\r\n   \"close_criterion\": \"S5 admission freezes its own subject, authority and evidence\",\r\n   \"closed_requires_fresh_verification\": true\r\n  